cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "London Transit Resilience System (LTRS): Visualising bus-route disruption and accessibility retention in London"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fan
    given-names: Yuxiang
    affiliation: "UCL Centre for Advanced Spatial Analysis"
  - family-names: Tao
    given-names: Siyan
    affiliation: "UCL Centre for Advanced Spatial Analysis"
date-released: 2026-04-30
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yuxiang2526/ltis-london-transit-immune-system"
url: "https://yuxiang2526.github.io/ltis-london-transit-immune-system/"
abstract: >
  LTRS is an interactive resilience visualisation built for the CASA0029
  Urban Data Visualisation module. It treats single bus-route disruption
  as a stress test on London's surface transport network, recomputing
  per-grid accessibility on the OSM walking network and visualising
  baseline accessibility, accessibility loss, retention and indicative
  exposure at both 100 m grid and LSOA scale across Greater London. The
  deliverable combines a React + TypeScript + MapLibre frontend with an
  embedded Mapbox GL JS scenario engine driven by a 543-route
  pre-computed loss matrix.
